:root{color-scheme:dark;font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#0d1722;color:#eaf3fb}main{max-width:1180px;margin:auto;padding:24px 16px 100px}h1{font-size:clamp(2rem,7vw,4rem);margin:12px 0}h2{font-size:1.35rem}p{color:#c1d0dd;line-height:1.64}a{color:#ffdd9b}button,input{font:inherit;padding:12px;border-radius:10px;color:#fff;background:#193343;border:1px solid #618598}input{width:100%}.tag{color:#edd39e;font-size:.75rem;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase}.stats,.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(205px,1fr));gap:10px}.panel,.card{background:#182d3b;border:1px solid #476578;border-radius:13px;padding:16px;margin:10px 0}.card{margin:0;background:#1b3545}.card b{display:block;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.card small{color:#c3d2e0;display:block;margin-top:6px}.small{font-size:.82rem}.hidden{display:none!important}:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #ffdb8f;outline-offset:2px}@media(max-width:620px){.stats,.cards{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.panel{padding:12px}}</style><script defer src="../shared/one-universal-v061.js"></script></head><body><main>
<a href="../">← TABOR FACTORY</a><div class="tag">NATHAN AI → TABOR ROOT → TABOR 1-2-3 FACTORY</div><h1>ONE · Universal System Atlas</h1><p>Every existing public browser app receives the same optional system controls; its own source, functionality, and original content remain intact. The full private Master Library, native iOS packages, external accounts, and unpublished assets are not automatically synchronized or published.</p>
<div class="stats"><section class="card"><b>54</b>Browser pages with shared interface</section><section class="card"><b>5</b>Named lifecycle eras</section><section class="card"><b>11</b>Scale levels · subatomic to cosmic</section><section class="card"><b>33</b>Library planning departments</section></div>
<section class="panel"><h2>The Five Eras / Errors Matrix</h2><div class="cards"><article class="card"><b>BCE · Before Component Engines</b><p>Preserve technical legacy, legacy hardcoding and archived components</p></article><article class="card"><b>BC · Before Code</b><p>Discovery, consent, wireframes, originality and documented scope</p></article><article class="card"><b>AC · Atomic &amp; Cosmic</b><p>Sub-pixels, tokens, components, pages, planets, ecosystem</p></article><article class="card"><b>CE · Component Era</b><p>Compilation, state, routing, testing, rendering and deployment preparation</p></article><article class="card"><b>AD · After Deployment</b><p>Explicitly consented diagnostics, support, repairs and user feedback</p></article></div><p class="small">“Eras / errors,” the Tower of Babel, and the end-of-world reading are the author’s interpretive framework. The software eras are project-specific labels; they are not established Biblical translations or a literal chronology.</p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>The 11-level scale</h2><div class="cards"><div class="card"><small>00</small><b>Subpixel &amp; display physics</b></div><div class="card"><small>01</small><b>Design tokens &amp; vector coordinates</b></div><div class="card"><small>02</small><b>Atoms</b></div><div class="card"><small>03</small><b>Molecules</b></div><div class="card"><small>04</small><b>Organisms</b></div><div class="card"><small>05</small><b>Templates</b></div><div class="card"><small>06</small><b>Pages</b></div><div class="card"><small>07</small><b>Applications / modules</b></div><div class="card"><small>08</small><b>Operating systems / platforms</b></div><div class="card"><small>09</small><b>Cross-app galaxy</b></div><div class="card"><small>10</small><b>ONE universe</b></div></div></section><section class="panel"><h2>The shared architecture</h2><div class="cards"><div class="card"><small>01</small><b>Identity, sovereignty and consent</b></div><div class="card"><small>02</small><b>Original-words preservation &amp; provenance</b></div><div class="card"><small>03</small><b>Design tokens</b></div><div class="card"><small>04</small><b>Fill</b></div><div class="card"><small>05</small><b>Wallpaper</b></div><div class="card"><small>06</small><b>Skin</b></div><div class="card"><small>07</small><b>Wireframes &amp; layout</b></div><div class="card"><small>08</small><b>Typography</b></div><div class="card"><small>09</small><b>Iconography</b></div><div class="card"><small>10</small><b>Chrome and navigation</b></div><div class="card"><small>11</small><b>Motion and feedback</b></div><div class="card"><small>12</small><b>Accessibility</b></div><div class="card"><small>13</small><b>Localization and direction</b></div><div class="card"><small>14</small><b>Application state</b></div><div class="card"><small>15</small><b>Offline data and imports</b></div><div class="card"><small>16</small><b>API and permission boundaries</b></div><div class="card"><small>17</small><b>Security and retention</b></div><div class="card"><small>18</small><b>Testing and release gates</b></div><div class="card"><small>19</small><b>Attention and device sovereignty</b></div><div class="card"><small>20</small><b>Universal search and master library</b></div><div class="card"><small>21</small><b>Opt-in diagnostics and privacy</b></div><div class="card"><small>22</small><b>Audits, continuity and rollback</b></div></div></section><section class="panel"><h2>All public app pages</h2><label for="search">Search by name or code path</label><input id="search" placeholder="Find a module, game, reader, factory, or source" autocomplete="off"><p id="count" aria-live="polite"></p><div id="pages" class="cards"></div></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Preservation and release gate</h2><p>This public code does not include private books or bank, medical, identity, or customer data. It does not turn on telemetry or install native apps. The shell is additive, optional and locally controlled. Native bundles will require separately packaged resource files.</p><p><a href="../one/">ONE The Last App</a> · <a href="../one/library/">Master Library</a> · <a href="../one/meet/">Meet People Where They Are</a> · <a href="https://github.com/NathanAIoxr/Nathan-AI-Sovereign-Core">Source code</a></p></section></main>
